          %title Weakly constant function
          %h1#weakly_constant_function Weakly constant function
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#relationship_to_constancy"} Relationship to constancy
              %li
                %a{:href => "#weakly_constant_endomaps"} Weakly constant endomaps
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            By a
            %em weakly constant function
            one means a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            which is equipped with a certain sort of “witness of
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constancy
          %p
            However, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"} Andrej Bauer
            but did not catch on.)
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f\colon A\to B
          %p
            is
            %em weakly constant
            if we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification+types"} identification types
            of all the values of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            on all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            of arguments:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\prod_{(x,y:A)}
                  (f x = f y)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By regarding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-category
            with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+products"} binary products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            is
            %em weakly constant
            if the two composites
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times A \rightrightarrows A \xrightarrow{f} B
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalent
          %h2#relationship_to_constancy Relationship to constancy
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
            in the sense that it factors through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            (i.e. we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi λ
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \lambda x. b
            for some
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is obviously weakly constant. The converse holds if we know that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} inhabited
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f a = f a_0
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            is weakly constant, yet not equal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda x.b
            for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mo ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:\varnothing
            (since no such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            exists).
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            factors through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+truncation"} propositional truncation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}
            are equal (i.e. it is an
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            factors through
            %em any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            (in which case it in fact also factors through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the latter).
          %p
            The converse to this last implication does hold for some specific
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                factors through the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncation"} 0-truncation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|_0}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
                of the two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projections"} projections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mn 0
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|_0} \times {\|A\|_0} \to {\|A\|_0}
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+truncation"} propositional truncation
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                has
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+support"} split support
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|} \to A \xrightarrow{f} B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is equal to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                by weak constancy.
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mi P
                        %mo +
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=P+Q
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-propositions"} h-propositions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo *
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P*Q
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                of the two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projections"} projections
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo ←
                        %mi P
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Q
                        %mo →
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \leftarrow P\times Q \to Q
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                of this pushout says exactly that any weakly constant map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo +
                      %mi Q
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P+Q\to B
                factors through
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo *
                        %mi Q
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi P
                        %mo +
                        %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P*Q = \Vert P+Q\Vert
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=B
                (see below).
          %p
            However, it can fail in general, even when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} merely
            inhabited (i.e.
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}= 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                  %mo +
                  %mi Q
                  %mo +
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=P+Q+R
            for h-propositions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            be the triple pushout of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            under
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\times Q
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\times R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q\times R
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|} = 1
            but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            has no
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a,b,c\}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P=\{a,b\}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q=\{b,c\}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R=\{a,c\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(S) = 1
            for all nonempty proper subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(\emptyset) = S^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            has no global sections.
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://groups.google.com/d/msg/homotopytypetheory/FeBAScTgwzg/Dx6E3-ezdxIJ"} this discussion
          %p
            In general, being weakly constant may be regarded as an “incoherent approximation” to constancy in the sense of factoring through an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times A\rightrightarrows A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+diagram"} simplicial diagram
            (the simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            of the map
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to 1
          %h2#weakly_constant_endomaps Weakly constant endomaps
          %p
            While an arbitrary weakly constant function is not very
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+law"} coherent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunction"} endofunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to A
            has some extra degree of “coherence”, as witnessed by the following results of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KECA"} (KECA)
          .un_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to A
              is weakly constant, then the type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fix(f) \coloneqq \sum_{x:A} (f x = x)
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Suppose
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H: \prod_{(x,y:A)} (f x = f y)
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi Fix
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,p),(b,q):Fix(f)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,p)=(b,q)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:a=b
              be the concatenated path
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %mi f
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %mi f
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                    %mi f
                    %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi q
                    %mi b
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \xrightarrow{p^{-1}} f a \xrightarrow{H_{a,a}^{-1}} f a \xrightarrow{H_{a,b}} f b \xrightarrow{q} b.
            %p
              It will suffice to show that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo •
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ap
                        %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \bullet r = ap_f(r) \bullet q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ap
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ap_f
              denotes the action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              on paths. However, the dependent action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              on paths implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                    %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi ap
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{x,y} \bullet ap_f(s) = H_{x,y'}
              for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
              and any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:y=y'
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ap
                        %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo •
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ap_f(r) = H_{a,a}^{-1} \bullet H_{a,b}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo •
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ap
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \bullet r = ap_f(r) \bullet q
              is immediate. Thus,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fix(f)
              is an h-proposition.
            %p
              Now we have a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:A\to Fix(f)
              defined by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x) \coloneqq (f x, H_{f x,x})
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo →
                      %mi Fix
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|} \to Fix(f)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi pr
                        %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi Fix
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pr_1:Fix(f) \to A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Fix
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fix(f) \to {\|A\|}
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+support"} split support
              if and only if it admits a weakly constant endomap
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to A
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|A\|} \to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to {\|A\|} \to \A
              is weakly constant. Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is steady,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fix(f) = {\|A\|}
              by the lemma, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi Fix
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pr_1:Fix(f) \to A
              splits the support of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Note that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pr
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pr_1 \circ g = f
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .un_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              A type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
              if and only if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=_A y
              admits a weakly constant endomap.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We know that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an h-set just when all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=_A y
              have split support.
